{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following PyPy 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original PyPy 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\ndef build_prime_list(max_val):\n    prime_list = []\n    for num in range(2, max_val):\n        prime_check = True\n        for p in prime_list:\n            if p * p > num:\n                break\n            if num % p == 0:\n                prime_check = False\n                break\n        if prime_check:\n            prime_list.append(num)\n    return prime_list\n\nprimes = build_prime_list(6000)\n\ndef get_prime_factors(n):\n    factor_counts = {}\n    for p in primes:\n        if p * p > n:\n            break\n        if n % p == 0:\n            count = 0\n            while n % p == 0:\n                n //= p\n                count += 1\n            factor_counts[p] = count\n    if n > 1:\n        factor_counts[n] = 1\n    return factor_counts\n\ndef list_divisors(n):\n    factors = get_prime_factors(n)\n    divisors = [1]\n    for prime, exp in factors.items():\n        extended = []\n        for d in divisors:\n            power = 1\n            for _ in range(exp + 1):\n                extended.append(d * power)\n                power *= prime\n        divisors = extended\n    return divisors\n\ndef compute_value(n, mod):\n    memo = {0: 0, 1: 1, 2: 2}\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        value = 2 * memo[i - 1]\n        for divisor in list_divisors(i):\n            if 2 <= divisor <= i:\n                value += memo[i // divisor] - memo[(i - 1) // divisor]\n                value %= mod\n        memo[i] = value % mod\n    return memo[n]\n\nn_input, m_input = map(int, input().split())\nprint(compute_value(n_input, m_input))\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <unordered_map>\n#include <cmath>\n\nstd::vector<int> build_prime_list(int max_val) {\n    std::vector<int> prime_list;\n    for (int num = 2; num < max_val; num++) {\n        bool prime_check = true;\n        for (int p : prime_list) {\n            if (p * p > num) {\n                break;\n            }\n            if (num % p == 0) {\n                prime_check = false;\n                break;\n            }\n        }\n        if (prime_check) {\n            prime_list.push_back(num);\n        }\n    }\n    return prime_list;\n}\n\nstd::vector<int> primes = build_prime_list(6000);\n\nstd::unordered_map<int, int> get_prime_factors(int n) {\n    std::unordered_map<int, int> factor_counts;\n    for (int p : primes) {\n        if (p * p > n) {\n            break;\n        }\n        if (n % p == 0) {\n            int count = 0;\n            while (n % p == 0) {\n                n /= p;\n                count++;\n            }\n            factor_counts[p] = count;\n        }\n    }\n    if (n > 1) {\n        factor_counts[n] = 1;\n    }\n    return factor_counts;\n}\n\nstd::vector<int> list_divisors(int n) {\n    auto factors = get_prime_factors(n);\n    std::vector<int> divisors = {1};\n    for (const auto& kv : factors) {\n        int prime = kv.first;\n        int exp = kv.second;\n        std::vector<int> extended;\n        for (int d : divisors) {\n            int power = 1;\n            for (int _ = 0; _ <= exp; _++) {\n                extended.push_back(d * power);\n                power *= prime;\n            }\n        }\n        divisors = extended;\n    }\n    return divisors;\n}\n\nint compute_value(int n, int mod) {\n    std::unordered_map<int, int> memo;\n    memo[0] = 0;\n    memo[1] = 1;\n    memo[2] = 2;\n    for (int i = 3; i <= n; i++) {\n        long long value = (2LL * memo[i - 1]) % mod;\n        auto divs = list_divisors(i);\n        for (int divisor : divs) {\n            if (2 <= divisor && divisor <= i) {\n                value += memo[i / divisor] - memo[(i - 1) / divisor];\n                value %= mod;\n                if (value < 0) value += mod;\n            }\n        }\n        memo[i] = value % mod;\n    }\n    return memo[n];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_input, m_input;\n    std::cin >> n_input >> m_input;\n    std::cout << compute_value(n_input, m_input) << std::endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.8053239627042785e-05, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -1.847726889536716e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.0411134250462055e-05, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.5033637939486653e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -4.529942543740617e-06, -0.37967801094055176, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00010895135346800089, -0.007606944534927607, -2.5629668016335927e-05, -0.04721122235059738, -0.01815476082265377, -0.632724404335022, 0.0, -4.410734163684538e-06, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -6.6756979322235566e-06, -0.03805174306035042, -0.0011767374817281961, -4.768370445162873e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -1.19209282445